          en: 'Investing in logic is investing in permanent professional portability. Languages emerge and disappear, frameworks are replaced every few years, paradigms evolve. But the ability to think logically, decompose problems, recognize patterns, and build structured solutions remains relevant throughout an entire career. The professional who prioritizes logical fundamentals over superficial mastery of multiple languages builds a foundation that supports any direction the career takes. and this foundation is the differentiator that separates adaptable professionals from disposable ones.',
