          en: 'In career terms, understanding all layers. even at different depths. significantly increases professional value. The frontend developer who understands backend makes smarter state and caching decisions. The backend developer who understands frontend designs APIs that are pleasant to consume. The professional who understands infrastructure delivers software that works in production, not just in demonstrations.\n\nIn the progression from junior to mid-level, the professional is expected to understand at least superficially the layers outside their specialty. In the progression from mid to senior, systemic vision spanning all layers is expected. In interviews for intermediate and senior positions, questions about how layers interact are increasingly common. The candidate who demonstrates understanding of the complete system differentiates significantly from those who only know their layer.',
