          en: 'Career progression in development is directly correlated with the level of systems thinking. The junior executes tasks. The mid-level understands how their tasks fit into the system. The senior designs and evolves the system. The staff engineer defines technical strategy considering multiple systems. Each level requires a broadening of vision: from code to component, component to service, service to system, system to ecosystem.\n\nIn interviews for intermediate and senior positions, the candidate is frequently evaluated on their ability to think in systems. Questions like "how would you design a notification system?" or "how would you migrate from a monolithic architecture to microservices?" directly test this competency. The candidate who responds focusing only on code demonstrates limitation. The one who responds considering scalability, resilience, monitoring, and migration strategy demonstrates maturity. Developing systems thinking early accelerates progression and opens doors to the market\'s most valued positions.',
